  "_what": "The content set each seedVersion names, APPEND-ONLY. seedVersion is stamped onto every seed module, and a stored seat type version is immutable, so (module, version) must resolve to ONE content set forever. Adding a record is the whole of an intentional content change: raise seedVersion in domain/seedmap/seedmap.go and run this package's tests with -update-seedcontent-lock. Editing a recorded set, or adding a record under a version that already has one, is the drift this file exists to refuse. SeedVersion 1.4.2 has no record here on purpose: it named TWO sets - the library as it stood when 42de79c2 raised the const to 1.4.2, and the same library after 39105865 changed two blocks under it - and recording either one would write down a claim that is false.",
